// D5: Secret Retrieval by a Static IAM User
// ATT&CK: T1552.004 (Unsecured Credentials: Private Keys)
//          T1555.006 (Credentials from Password Stores: Cloud Secrets Manager)
// Data Source: AWSCloudTrail
// Logic: GetSecretValue (not List/DescribeSecret) whose access key is a
//   long-lived user key (AKIA prefix) rather than a role session key (ASIA).
//   In most environments, secrets are read by roles, never by static users.
// FP Assessment: Rare. Any static-user secret retrieval is worth investigating.
// Hunt 24 — TideGlass | Jenna Frank

AWSCloudTrail
| where EventName == "GetSecretValue"          // the retrieval call, not List/Describe
| where UserIdentityAccessKeyId startswith "AKIA"   // long-lived IAM user key, not an ASIA role session
| project TimeGenerated, UserIdentityAccessKeyId, SourceIpAddress, UserAgent, ResponseElements
